.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt LP 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm lp
.Nd send files to a printer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c
.Op Fl d Ar dest
.Op Fl n Ar copies
.Op Fl msw
.Op Fl o Ar option
.Op Fl t Ar title
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility submits a POSIX print request.
It parses the Issue 8 options, resolves the destination, and writes the input documents to a
local output destination.
.Pp
RavenBSD has no print daemon and no network print service.
A destination that is an absolute path or an explicit scheme path, such as
.Pa /dev/lp0
or
.Pa tty:console ,
is opened for writing and the request is written synchronously.
The destination must already exist;
.Nm
never creates it.
Every other destination is a logical printer name.
No service exists behind such a name, so
.Nm
reports it as unavailable and exits 1.
It never reports a successful print when no destination is available.
.Pp
If no
.Ar file
operand is given, or an operand is
.Ql - ,
standard input is read.
In the target image standard input is the console.
.Pp
No request ID is written to standard output: there is no spooler and the local write is
synchronous.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
Copy the input before writing.
The client always reads each document fully into memory, so a successful completion means no
further access to the input files is required.
.It Fl d Ar dest
Select the destination.
This option takes precedence over
.Ev LPDEST ,
which takes precedence over
.Ev PRINTER .
An empty environment value is treated as unset.
.It Fl n Ar copies
Write
.Ar copies
complete document sequences.
.Ar copies
must be a positive decimal integer.
Every file is written as an integral whole.
.It Fl m
Send mail after the files have been printed.
The option is accepted, but this image has no mail transport and no mail is sent.
.It Fl o Ar option
Pass a printer-dependent option.
The option is accepted and kept in request order.
A local file or device has no device-dependent options.
.It Fl s
Suppress informative messages.
Diagnostics still go to standard error.
.It Fl t Ar title
Use
.Ar title
on the banner page.
The option is accepted, but no banner page is generated for a synchronous local write.
.It Fl w
After a successful write, print
.Dq lp: request printed on '<dest>'
to standard error unless
.Fl s
is also given.
.El
.Sh OPERANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar file
A pathname of a file to output.
If no operands are specified, or an operand is
.Ql - ,
standard input is used.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev LPDEST
The destination when
.Fl d
is not specified.
.It Ev PRINTER
The destination when neither
.Fl d
nor
.Ev LPDEST
is specified.
.El
.Pp
The standard
.Ev LANG ,
.Ev LC_ALL ,
.Ev LC_CTYPE ,
.Ev LC_MESSAGES
and
.Ev LC_TIME
variables affect the C-locale client in the usual way.
The image currently provides the C locale only.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
The exit status is 0 only when a local destination accepted the complete request.
It is 1 when no destination is configured, a destination is unavailable, or an input or write
error occurs.
A usage error exits 2.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bd -literal -offset indent
lp: no print destination configured
lp: destination '<dest>' is not available
lp: destination '<dest>' is not available: <reason>
.Ed
.Pp
The first line is used when
.Fl d ,
.Ev LPDEST
and
.Ev PRINTER
are all unset or empty.
The second line is used for a logical printer name, and the third for a local path that cannot
be opened or written.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mailx 1
.Sh STANDARDS
IEEE Std 1003.1-2024
.Pq POSIX.1-2024 .
.Sh CAVEATS
No request ID is printed and no banner page is generated.
The
.Fl m
option sends no mail, and
.Fl o
options have no effect on a plain local file or device.
Input documents are held in memory.
